WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.207
A software update left some Australian Tesla owners without home power after their vehicle stopped exporting to the grid. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 658. After that, a New York permit stall, first principles on home storage and musk on optimus leasing. Owners reported to the driven that their home batteries went offline after the change. Vehicle to home export that had previously let excess solar or stored energy support household loads no longer does that job. A New York homeowner,

00:00:30.207 --> 00:00:35.907
Tech Insider reports paid a $70 permit fee out of pocket after Tesla filed the replacement

00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:37.327
application without payment.

00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:42.747
The three affected units, two Powerwall Plus packs equipped with solar inverters and one

00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:45.807
Powerwall 2, have been deactivated since August.

00:00:46.487 --> 00:00:49.447
The permit lists Powerwall 3 hardware as the replacement.

00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:54.487
The owner covered the fee to avoid another month or two of delay if the application bounced

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.827
back to Tesla for payment.

00:00:55.827 --> 00:01:00.827
Until the replacement is complete, the homeowner cannot turn to the batteries after sunset

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:05.127
or during an outage, even though the rooftop panels keep producing electricity.

00:01:06.339 --> 00:01:10.499
Municipal permitting offices still treat battery swaps like new construction filings.

00:01:10.999 --> 00:01:14.939
Hardware can improve, and the replacement path can even root through newer equipment,

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:17.739
and that administrative layer still sits in the way.

00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:23.039
Residential storage economics now hinge on permitting speed as much as on pack price.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:28.439
A stall measured in months means loss, solar, self-consumption, and loss backup capacity

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:29.279
during outages.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:32.719
Those costs compound faster than the filing fee itself.

00:01:33.279 --> 00:01:37.639
When the installer leaves the payment line blank, the customer absorbs both the cash

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.159
outlay and the time risk.

00:01:39.559 --> 00:01:44.779
That shift pushes the effective cost of ownership up even before any hardware pricing is considered.

00:01:45.379 --> 00:01:49.759
The newer hardware on the replacement path also changes the long-term service profile

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:50.299
for the home.

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:55.719
Over time, these frictions cap how quickly distributed storage can scale as a grid resource.

00:01:56.179 --> 00:02:00.739
Each extra week of downtime reduces the value proposition for the next buyer weighing

00:02:00.739 --> 00:02:03.099
a power wall against simpler backup options.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:07.779
The pattern repeats across municipalities that still treat battery replacements like

00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:08.979
new construction permits.

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:14.499
Closing that gap requires either Tesla to prepay every filing or local rules that treat

00:02:14.499 --> 00:02:18.259
like for like swaps as administrative updates rather than fresh reviews.

00:02:18.259 --> 00:02:23.699
The amount is small in isolation, yet the cumulative effect across thousands of similar

00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:27.419
cases shapes the real delivered cost of residential energy storage.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:32.579
Faster permitting would directly improve the payback period for solar-plus storage systems.

00:02:33.139 --> 00:02:37.799
It would also increase the number of households that can justify the investment on purely economic

00:02:37.799 --> 00:02:38.239
grounds.

